# Sanket Vaanni mobile — environment example
#
# Copy to `.env` in apps/mobile and adjust. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not.
#   PowerShell:  Copy-Item .env.example .env
#
# Changing API_BASE_URL is a CONFIGURATION change, not a code change. After
# editing, restart Metro with a cache reset:
#   npm start -- --reset-cache
#
# There are NO secrets in this project. Do not put any here — anything prefixed
# with REACT_NATIVE_/EXPO_PUBLIC_ or read via @env is inlined into the bundle
# and is therefore effectively public.

# Base URL of the Sanket Vaanni backend (apps/backend).
#
#   Android emulator  -> http://10.0.2.2:4000   (host loopback alias)
#   Physical device   -> http://<your-host-LAN-IP>:4000
#                        (find it with: ipconfig  — and run the backend with
#                         HOST=0.0.0.0 so it accepts connections from the phone)
#   iOS simulator     -> http://127.0.0.1:4000
#
# If unset, development falls back to the emulator/simulator default and
# production resolves to "not configured". The app works offline either way.
API_BASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2:4000
